        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willisburg%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city expanded in the 1870s as a crossroads community at the intersection of two turnpikes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willisburg%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Willisburg is concentrated along Kentucky Route 433 (Main Street), mostly in the vicinity of its intersection with Kentucky Route 53, west of Harrodsburg and northeast of Springfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willisburg%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Willisburg Lake, an impoundment of Lick Creek built by the city in the late 1960s, lies just to the northwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willisburg%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
